From acc5ccf31835536d3f148ad242b523364d2e517e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gaia <build@heygaia.io>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 07:40:09 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] fix(js): a script the watchdog terminates no longer wedges
 the scripts behind it

A fetched dynamic script reports its completion through a callback the
engine calls after running it. When the watchdog terminated one (a runaway
script past its budget) the callback never ran: the in-order queue stayed
busy, every later in-order and module script never executed, and the
load-delaying count never dropped, so the page reported pending scripts
forever. Script runs in flight are now tracked, and after any cancelled
termination (command watchdog, task budget, heap limit) the runtime
settles them in every realm.

Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Tm2SNEJ42hMPiZ6cFb8Vih
